  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: No experiments have been completed, so there is no prior information about which modality, encoder, or fusion strategy is effective. The most fundamental uncertainty is whether either single modality alone provides a useful signal, and what performance floor we should expect. 2) What this tests: config_011 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50, no aggregation, no fusion) is the simplest possible configuration in the search space. It isolates the contribution of the image modality with a well-understood encoder and no additional complexity, establishing a clean single-modality baseline. 3) Why it is the best first experiment: Under a limited budget, establishing a clear performance floor with the fewest confounding design choices is the highest-information first step. It gives a reference point against which every subsequent multimodal or RNA-only experiment can be judged. If image-only performance is already strong, multimodal experiments must clear a high bar; if it is weak, it motivates exploring RNA or fusion. This simple anchor also makes later ablations (e.g., adding RNA, changing encoder, adding aggregation) interpretable because they differ from this baseline in exactly one dimension."
